<title>MALAYSIA: Nauticalink in Philippines ferry deal.</title>
<headline>Nauticalink in Philippines ferry deal.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian ferry operator Nauticalink Bhd said it has agreed to form a joint-venture that would run a passenger ferry operation in East Malaysia's Sabah state and southern Philippines.</p>
<p>The venture is between Nauticalink unit Wajaragam Sdn Bhd and International Sandblast Marketing Corp, a unit of Philippines' Tawi Tawi Shipping Corp.</p>
<p>Nauticalink would own 40 percent of the venture, with International Sandblast holding the balance.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603 230 8911)</p>
</text>
